{"actor":{"display":"Evin Tunador","id":"evintunador@gmail.com","type":"human"},"content":{"blocks":[{"content":"1\t---\n2\tname: project-cledger-gemini-qwen-adapters\n3\tdescription: \"gemini-cli + qwen-code adapters shipped 0.20.0 (PR #5, draft); gemini WAL union-capture decision, qwen headless hook kill, torn-line cursor fix\"\n4\tmetadata: \n5\t  node_type: memory\n6\t  type: project\n7\t  originSessionId: 8f1a9339-b2b4-4bad-b2a9-3123e47d2a77\n8\t  modified: 2026-08-04T04:51:28.607Z\n9\t---\n10\t\n11\tAdapters for Gemini CLI and Qwen Code, 0.20.0, PR #5 (draft, branch\n12\t`worktree-more-cli-adapters`). Both CLIs were npm-installed globally and driven\n13\tagainst the local ds4-gateway (`http://127.0.0.1:9002/v1`, OpenAI-compatible,\n14\tmodel `deepseek-v4-flash`) to produce real sessions — that endpoint is the cheap\n15\tway to generate real transcripts for any OpenAI-compatible CLI without accounts.\n16\tGemini CLI does *not* accept an OpenAI base URL; its format was pinned from its\n17\tshipped (unminified) bundle at `/opt/homebrew/lib/node_modules/@google/gemini-cli/bundle/`.\n18\t\n19\tDecisions worth remembering:\n20\t\n21\t- **Gemini's session file is a write-ahead log, not a transcript.** Records:\n22\t  `$rewindTo` removal, bare message upsert by durable id, `$set` metadata patch\n23\t  (a `$set.messages` array replaces the whole document), and the\n24\t  `sessionId`+`projectHash` header. Verified: after a failed API call Gemini\n25\t  wrote a snapshot that dropped the prompt the user had just typed. So capture\n26\t  takes the **union** of every message ever written (last value wins) rather\n27\t  than replaying removals — deletions are recorded in `GeminiSession.rewound`\n28\t  instead. Side benefit: `seq` assigned at first sighting is never reused, so\n29\t  rewinds can't renumber later turns (better than opencode's positional seq).\n30\t- **Qwen headless mode kills hooks.** `qwen -p` fires `Stop` then exits,\n31\t  tearing down the hook process. Instant hooks survive; a git-notes append does\n32\t  not. Fix: `install` appends `>/dev/null 2>&1` to the command, which reliably\n33\t  works but costs visible drift warnings. Same trade the opencode plugin makes.\n34\t  Upstream fix would be to await the hook.\n35\t- **Torn trailing line bug (pre-existing, fixed here).** claude-code and codex\n36\t  advanced the cursor to `lines.length` even when the last line was half\n37\t  written, permanently losing that turn. All line-based adapters now hold the\n38\t  cursor at the first unparseable line.\n39\t- Gemini `info`/`error`/`warning` UI notices are skipped, and a rewind is not\n40\t  itself recorded as an event — both left as Roadmap items because they are\n41\t  schema questions, not adapter ones.\n42\t\n43\tOverlaps [[project-cledger-full-capture]] (PR #4, 0.19.0) in the three existing\n44\tadapters; whichever merges second needs a rebase. See also\n45\t[[project-cledger-opencode-adapter]] for the adapter conventions both follow.\n46\t","tool_use_id":"toolu_01CfsvCBjMRkJ9GgikY1xFoD","type":"tool_result"}],"role":"user"},"context":{"branch":"worktree-capture-everything","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger/.claude/worktrees/capture-everything","head":"af5de76a51a896338d095b5795f19b4a402eb0c7","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/conversation-ledger.git"},"conversation":{"id":"claude-code:bb4f0d43-d543-48ee-8428-5bf2dafa4ade","seq":395},"id":"ev1-3be353aa079baf1288ea1319e2eaec26b634ecbf9c523a9cf3940bd861cf4c79","kind":"conversation_turn","occurred_at":"2026-08-06T00:58:43.219Z","producer":{"session_id":"bb4f0d43-d543-48ee-8428-5bf2dafa4ade","source":"claude-code","source_version":"2.1.222","tool":"cledger","version":"0.18.0"},"raw":{"data":{"cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger/.claude/worktrees/capture-everything","entrypoint":"cli","gitBranch":"worktree-capture-everything","isSidechain":false,"message":{"content":[{"content":"1\t---\n2\tname: project-cledger-gemini