{"actor":{"display":"Evin Tunador","id":"evintunador@gmail.com","type":"human"},"content":{"blocks":[{"content":"The file /Users/evintunador/.claude/projects/-Users-evintunador-repos-evintunador-conversation-ledger/memory/project-cledger-full-capture.md has been updated successfully.","tool_use_id":"toolu_01Bunknakaj4535GCLVguHjy","type":"tool_result"}],"role":"user"},"context":{"branch":"worktree-capture-everything","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger/.claude/worktrees/capture-everything","head":"af5de76a51a896338d095b5795f19b4a402eb0c7","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/conversation-ledger.git"},"conversation":{"id":"claude-code:bb4f0d43-d543-48ee-8428-5bf2dafa4ade","seq":391},"id":"ev1-39828899e9c39d90e10f00903f7c565caefb9d97776cf9794b6307d43623c21c","kind":"conversation_turn","occurred_at":"2026-08-06T00:58:33.329Z","producer":{"session_id":"bb4f0d43-d543-48ee-8428-5bf2dafa4ade","source":"claude-code","source_version":"2.1.222","tool":"cledger","version":"0.18.0"},"raw":{"data":{"cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger/.claude/worktrees/capture-everything","entrypoint":"cli","gitBranch":"worktree-capture-everything","isSidechain":false,"message":{"content":[{"content":"The file /Users/evintunador/.claude/projects/-Users-evintunador-repos-evintunador-conversation-ledger/memory/project-cledger-full-capture.md has been updated successfully.","tool_use_id":"toolu_01Bunknakaj4535GCLVguHjy","type":"tool_result"}],"role":"user"},"parentUuid":"320e0a4d-6838-44b7-ac40-820e7c55724a","promptId":"afb6a096-bf02-410d-9b2a-54cf1e4372db","sessionId":"bb4f0d43-d543-48ee-8428-5bf2dafa4ade","sessionKind":"bg","session_id":"9a01c126-8f0a-4060-95f9-fe3a00a2a8c3","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"320e0a4d-6838-44b7-ac40-820e7c55724a","timestamp":"2026-08-06T00:58:33.329Z","toolUseResult":{"filePath":"/Users/evintunador/.claude/projects/-Users-evintunador-repos-evintunador-conversation-ledger/memory/project-cledger-full-capture.md","memdirStamped":true,"newString":"**The tail sweep needed a scope bound** (commit `af5de76`, found by reviewing against the real `~/.claude/projects` corpus rather than fixtures). As first written it adopted *every* transcript in the project dir with no cursor and no recency bound: 6,973 events spanning three weeks, all anchored to a HEAD created that minute. **A missing cursor means \"never captured\", not \"has a gap\"** — the sweep now skips those, and `readCursor` returns `null` rather than a zeroed cursor so a cursor legitimately at line 0 stays distinguishable. Same hook, same corpus afterwards: 1,496 events, 0.3s instead of 11.2s. Three more fixed in that commit: a torn final line was skipped permanently (cursor now stops short of an *unterminated* last line and records that line's byte offset, not the file size — recording the size would tell the next sweep nothing changed); cursors write temp-file-and-rename now that a sweep gives them a second writer; and `convertLine`'s empty-string session-id fallback disagreed with the record/preserve paths' filename fallback, so one line could land in two conversations depending on which branch read it.\n\n**Generalizable:** a capture pass that \"closes gaps\" must be scoped to what it already tracks — otherwise it silently becomes a backfill, and backfill anchored to current HEAD is a false statement about when a conversation happened.\n\n**Left open (now in the README roadmap):**","oldString":"**Left open (now in the README roadmap):**","originalFile":"---\nname: project-cledger-full-capture\ndescription: \"0.19.0 (PR #4, merged 2026-08-06) removed the per-adapter skip lists; four new record kinds, ConversationRef.parent, EvidenceEvent.resolved, the tail-sweep scope bound, and what was deliberately left out\"\nmetadata: \n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: 9a01c126-8f0a-4060-95f9-fe3a00a2a8c3\n  modified: 2026-08-06T00:58:25.218Z\n---\n\nShipped as 0.19.0 on branch `worktree-capture-everything`; **PR #4 merged to main 2026-08-06** as `666888f`.\n\n**What changed.** The `KNOWN_SKIPPED_LINE_TYPES` / `KNOWN_SKIPPED_PART_TYPES` lists are gone from all three adapters. Four new kinds in `KNOWN_KINDS`: `session_state` (declaration holding until restated), `activity` (point-in-time occurrence that is not a turn), `context_injection` (harness-inserted context material), `file_snapshot` (intermediate file state). Builders live in `src/adapters/records.ts`, the counterpart to `drift.ts`. One content shape everywhere: `*_type` discriminator (spread *last*, so a source field cannot clobber it) + source field names verbatim + `blocks` for prose.\n\n**Decisions worth remembering:**\n\n- The only surviving skip is codex `event_msg` payload types `agent_message`/`user_message` — genuine duplicates of a `response_item`. Everything else in `event_msg` (token counts, task lifecycle, sub-agent activity, aborts) has no twin and is `activity`.\n- Claude Code `system` lines split on **whether `content` is a non-empty string**, not on a subtype list: text means the user read it, so it is a `conversation_turn` with actor `system`. A subtype list would go stale.\n- `EvidenceEvent.resolved` is a new top-level field, **outside the identity subset**, holding capture-time resolution of machine-local pointers (today: sha256 + bytes of a Claude Code file-history backup). Digests only, never file bodies — the redaction stack walks `content`/`raw.data`, not this.\n- `ConversationRef.parent` is **inside** identity. Claude sidechains become `claude-code:<session>#agent:<agentId>`; opencode subagent sessions keep their own id and gain a parent.\n- opencode child sessions are discoverable *only* via the parent's `task` tool part `state.metadata.sessionId` — `opencode session list` returns top-level sessions only. Capture recurses depth-first with a `visited` guard.\n- Claude Code stores subagents two ways depending on version: inline `isSidechain` lines, and separate `<session>/subagents/agent-*.jsonl` files. `fileHistoryDir` therefore walks up to the `projects` directory instead of counting `dirname` calls.\n- `renormalize` upgrades previously-`unrecognized` non-turn lines into their record kind with id fidelity (tested), but **deliberately excludes `file_snapshot`** — the backup cache is long pruned by then, so the upgrade would displace a resolvable line with a digest-less record.\n- Display is separate from capture: `SESSION_MACHINERY_KINDS` are hidden from `log`/`show`/`conversations` behind `--with-state`. Sources restate mode/tracked-files far more often than anyone speaks.\n\n**Two bugs a live install found that replaying saved transcripts could not** (fixed in the second commit on the branch):\n\n1. **Subagent transcripts were never read.** Newer Claude Code writes subagents to `<session>/subagents/agent-<id>.jsonl` — a sibling file the hook payload never names. Sidechain *conversion* worked; nothing opened the file. Capture now walks that directory depth-first. Always check the transcript **directory**, not just the path the hook hands you.\n2. **A session cannot capture its own final lines.** The last hook reads to EOF, then Claude Code writes the closing bookkeeping — including the session's most complete `file-history-snapshot`. Observed: cursor at line 40 of a 50-line transcript, the only snapshot naming a real backup at line 49. Fixed with a size-gated catch-up sweep over other transcripts in the project on each hook (cursors gained a `size` field). Still a workaround — a repo whose last session is never followed by another keeps an uncaptured tail.\n\nMeasured on the session that found both: 21 events before, 40 after.\n\n**Left open (now in the README roadmap):** capturing file *content* rather than just digests (wants a size policy + opt-in); codex `agent_message` embedded `encrypted_content` blocks still dropped rather than sealed; whether codex writes separate rollouts for sub-agents is unconfirmed, so codex sub-agent internals may still be unrecorded.\n\nRelated: [[project-cledger-opencode-adapter]], [[project-cledger-reasoning-preservation]], [[project-ledger-ecosystem]].\n","replaceAll":false,"structuredPatch":[{"lines":["   node_type: memory","   type: project","   originSessionId: 9a01c126-8f0a-4060-95f9-fe3a00a2a8c3","-  modified: 2026-08-06T00:58:25.218Z","+  modified: 2026-08-06T00:58:33.325Z"," ---"," "," Shipped as 0.19.0 on branch `worktree-capture-everything`; **PR #4 merged to main 2026-08-06** as `666888f`."],"newLines":7,"newStart":5,"oldLines":7,"oldStart":5},{"lines":[" "," Measured on the session that found both: 21 events before, 40 after."," ","+**The tail sweep needed a scope bound** (commit `af5de76`, found by reviewing against the real `~/.claude/projects` corpus rather than fixtures). As first written it adopted *every* transcript in the project dir with no cursor and no recency bound: 6,973 events spanning three weeks, all anchored to a HEAD created that minute. **A missing cursor means \"never captured\", not \"has a gap\"** — the sweep now skips those, and `readCursor` returns `null` rather than a zeroed cursor so a cursor legitimately at line 0 stays distinguishable. Same hook, same corpus afterwards: 1,496 events, 0.3s instead of 11.2s. Three more fixed in that commit: a torn final line was skipped permanently (cursor now stops short of an *unterminated* last line and records that line's byte offset, not the file size — recording the size would tell the next sweep nothing changed); cursors write temp-file-and-rename now that a sweep gives them a second writer; and `convertLine`'s empty-string session-id fallback disagreed with the record/preserve paths' filename fallback, so one line could land in two conversations depending on which branch read it.","+","+**Generalizable:** a capture pass that \"closes gaps\" must be scoped to what it already tracks — otherwise it silently becomes a backfill, and backfill anchored to current HEAD is a false statement about when a conversation happened.","+"," **Left open (now in the README roadmap):** capturing file *content* rather than just digests (wants a size policy + opt-in); codex `agent_message` embedded `encrypted_content` blocks still dropped rather than sealed; whether codex writes separate rollouts for sub-agents is unconfirmed, so codex sub-agent internals may still be unrecorded."," "," Related: [[project-cledger-opencode-adapter]], [[project-cledger-reasoning-preservation]], [[project-ledger-ecosystem]]."],"newLines":10,"newStart":30,"oldLines":6,"oldStart":30}],"userModified":false},"type":"user","userType":"external","uuid":"ab6feeea-dda7-4b1c-a987-12c67abc7fc8","version":"2.1.222"},"format":"claude-code-jsonl/1"},"recorded_at":"2026-08-06T00:59:28.260Z","schema":"conversation-ledger/v1"}
