en-adapters.md","memdirStamped":true,"newString":"- **Torn trailing line bug (pre-existing, fixed here).** claude-code and codex\n  advanced the cursor to `lines.length` even when the last line was half\n  written, permanently losing that turn. All line-based adapters now hold the\n  cursor at the first unparseable line.\n  **Reconcile on rebase:** PR #4's `af5de76` fixed this for claude-code only,\n  and more narrowly — it holds the cursor *only* at an unterminated final line\n  (`!raw.endsWith(\"\\n\") && i === lines.length - 1`), because holding at the\n  first unparseable line anywhere stalls a session's capture forever on real\n  mid-file corruption. Prefer the narrow rule, and extend it to codex + the two\n  new adapters, which PR #4 did not touch. It also records the held line's byte\n  offset as the cursor `size` rather than the file size — the sweep is size-\n  gated, so recording the file size would strand the very line held back.","oldString":"- **Torn trailing line bug (pre-existing, fixed here).** claude-code and codex\n  advanced the cursor to `lines.length` even when the last line was half\n  written, permanently losing that turn. All line-based adapters now hold the\n  cursor at the first unparseable line.","originalFile":"---\nname: project-cledger-gemini-qwen-adapters\ndescription: \"gemini-cli + qwen-code adapters shipped 0.20.0 (PR #5, draft); gemini WAL union-capture decision, qwen headless hook kill, torn-line cursor fix\"\nmetadata: \n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: 8f1a9339-b2b4-4bad-b2a9-3123e47d2a77\n  modified: 2026-08-04T04:51:28.607Z\n---\n\nAdapters for Gemini CLI and Qwen Code, 0.20.0, PR #5 (draft, branch\n`worktree-more-cli-adapters`). Both CLIs were npm-installed globally and driven\nagainst the local ds4-gateway (`http://127.0.0.1:9002/v1`, OpenAI-compatible,\nmodel `deepseek-v4-flash`) to produce real sessions — that endpoint is the cheap\nway to generate real transcripts for any OpenAI-compatible CLI without accounts.\nGemini CLI does *not* accept an OpenAI base URL; its format was pinned from its\nshipped (unminified) bundle at `/opt/homebrew/lib/node_modules/@google/gemini-cli/bundle/`.\n\nDecisions worth remembering:\n\n- **Gemini's session file is a write-ahead log, not a transcript.** Records:\n  `$rewindTo` removal, bare message upsert by durable id, `$set` metadata patch\n  (a `$set.messages` array replaces the whole document), and the\n  `sessionId`+`projectHash` header. Verified: after a failed API call Gemini\n  wrote a snapshot that dropped the prompt the user had just typed. So capture\n  takes the **union** of every message ever written (last value wins) rather\n  than replaying removals — deletions are recorded in `GeminiSession.rewound`\n  instead. Side benefit: `seq` assigned at first sighting is never reused, so\n  rewinds can't renumber later turns (better than opencode's positional seq).\n- **Qwen headless mode kills hooks.** `qwen -p` fires `Stop` then exits,\n  tearing down the hook process. Instant hooks survive; a git-notes append does\n  not. Fix: `install` appends `>/dev/null 2>&1` to the command, which reliably\n  works but costs visible drift warnings. Same trade the opencode plugin makes.\n  Upstream fix would be to await the hook.\n- **Torn trailing line bug (pre-existing, fixed here).** claude-code and codex\n  advanced the cursor to `lines.length` even when the last line was half\n  written, permanently losing that turn. All line-based adapters now hold the\n  cursor at the first unparseable line.\n- Gemini `info`/`error`/`warning` UI notices are skipped, and a rewind is not\n  itself recorded as an event — both left as Roadmap items because they are\n  schema questions, not adapter ones.\n\nOverlaps [[project-cledger-full-capture]] (PR #4, 0.19.0) in the three existing\nadapters; whichever merges second needs a rebase. See also\n[[project-cledger-opencode-adapter]] for the adapter conventions both follow.\n","replaceAll":false,"struct