{"actor":{"id":"claude-opus-5","type":"agent"},"content":{"blocks":[{"caller":{"type":"direct"},"id":"toolu_01TjZ2oxv2MaWsHTavc81sUV","input":{"content":"claude-code: bound the tail sweep to sessions cledger already tracks\n\nReview of the sweep against real transcripts, rather than the fixtures the\ntests use, turned up a scope it was never meant to have. The intent is stated\nin the commit that added it: a session cannot capture its own last lines, so\nthe *next* session in the repo closes that gap. A gap is a handful of lines,\nminutes old, and anchoring them to current HEAD is honest.\n\nWhat the code did was sweep every transcript in the project directory with no\ncursor and no recency bound. Measured on this repo's own project directory:\n6,973 events spanning three weeks of conversations, every one of them stamped\nwith a HEAD created that minute — sessions that predated the install, adopted\nsilently, anchored to a commit they were never about. That is a backfill\nwearing a gap-closer's clothes, and it is the kind of thing the ledger exists\nto not do.\n\nThe sweep now skips a transcript with no cursor. A missing cursor does not\nmean \"this session has a gap\", it means cledger never captured this session at\nall. `readCursor` returns null rather than a zeroed cursor so the two cases\nstay distinguishable — a cursor legitimately resting at line 0 is not the same\nfact. Same corpus, same hook: 1,496 events for the session that actually\nfired, 0.3s instead of 11.2s, and the gap-closing path still closes gaps.\n\nThree things found alongside it:\n\nA torn final line was lost for good. The last line of a transcript being\nwritten is half-flushed JSON; parsing failed, the line was skipped, and the\ncursor still advanced past it. Pre-existing, but the sweep goes looking for\ntails on purpose, which is exactly where torn lines live. The cursor now stops\nshort of an unterminated final line, and records the byte offset that line\nstarts at rather than the file size — recording the size would tell the next\nsweep nothing had changed and strand the very line held back. A parse failure\nanywhere else is real corruption and is still skipped, because holding the\ncursor there would stall the session forever.\n\nCursors have two writers now — a session's own hook, and any other session\nsweeping it. Written via temp file and rename, so a concurrent reader sees one\ncursor or the other and never a half-written file that parses as \"none\".\n\n`convertLine` fell back to an empty session id where the record and\npreservation paths fall back to the transcript's filename, so one line could\nland in `claude-code:` or `claude-code:<file>` depending only on which branch\nread it. They now agree. Confirmed live: lines without their own `sessionId`\nexist in real transcripts and now join the conversation they belong to.\n\nAlso drops opencode's private copy of the capture-tally merge helper in favour\nof the shared `mergeCaptureResult`.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011yyjMrYMdcPPiKnPmUm8Hs\n","file_path":"/Users/evintunador/.claude/jobs/9a01c126/tmp/msg.txt"},"name":"Write","type":"tool_use"}],"role":"assistant"},"context":{"branch":"worktree-capture-everything","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger/.claude/worktrees/capture-everything","head":"af5de76a51a896338d095b5795f19b4a402eb0c7","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/conversation-ledger.git"},"conversation":{"id":"claude-code:bb4f0d43-d543-48ee-8428-5bf2dafa4ade","seq":344},"id":"ev1-0e6cfa0bdef062355068426acee802fa0df11bb50f038a2354961d270acc0d62","kind":"conversation_turn","occurred_at":"2026-08-06T00:56:06.980Z","producer":{"model":"claude-opus-5","session_id":"bb4f0d43-d543-48ee-8428-5bf2dafa4ade","source":"claude-code","source_version":"2.1.222","tool":"cledger","version":"0.18.0"},"raw":{"data":{"cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger/.claude/wo